{"resourceIdentifier":"3166","resourceName":"ReforesTerra Grouped Project","description":"The ReforesTerra grouped project aims to recover low-intensity and degraded pasturelands in the Baixo Rio Jamari watershed in the State of Rondônia, Brazil, in the Southern Amazon region. The first project activity instance consists of the reforestation of 2,000 hectares in smallholdings. Available data indicates a potential for reforestation over 20,000 hectares in the watershed.\r\n\r\nThrough the reforestation of degraded lands in Permanent Protection Areas (PPAs) surrounding water bodies and in Legal Reserves (LRs) in other areas of the engaged landholdings, the grouped project aims to protect water resources and reintroduce native tree species. Additionally, the project is expected to benefit to 600 landholders in the first instance through capacity building and Payment for Ecosystem Services, as well as employing 37 local people full time and 12 other professionals in the region part time, with equal job opportunities for women and men. The first project activity instance will remove 805,304 tCO2e over the 30-year crediting period.","location":{"latitude":-9.450792,"longitude":-63.136370},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2024-05-24","endExclusive":"2024-06-24","endInclusive":"2024-06-23"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3166"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"State of Rondônia"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ReforesTerra – Restauração de Ecossistemas Florestais Ltda"},{"type":"string","value":"São Paulo, Brazil"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"24516"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and 